<title>CANADA: Imperial Oil cuts posted oil prices.</title>
<headline>Imperial Oil cuts posted oil prices.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Imperial Oil Ltd said on Tuesday it lowered the price it would pay for some grades of crude oil by C$6.00/cubic metre or C$0.95/barrel, effective immediately.</p>
<p>The new prices were listed as follows:</p>
<p>Edmonton light sweet C$180.00/cubic metre, or C$28.62/barrel</p>
<p>Cromer light sour C$168.00/cubic metre, or C$26.71/barrel</p>
<p>Bow River at Hardisty C$135.00/cubic metre, or C$21.46/barrel</p>
<p>Midale at Cromer C$150.00/cubic metre, or C$23.85/barrel</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
